# Every text file is committed with LF and checked out with LF on every host (the webgpu-graph-algorithms host
# lane runs its tests on a windows-latest checkout; its source-entry test and prettier assume LF). The two import
# corpora keep their own line endings (seven of their files are CRLF on purpose), and binary fixtures are marked so.
* text=auto eol=lf
graph-io/test/corpus/** -text
graphty-element/test/helpers/corpus/** -text
*.gsnp binary
*.png binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary

# Conformance fixtures are test inputs: store their bytes exactly (line endings, encodings, BOMs).
graph-io/test/conformance/fixtures/** -text -diff
# The official schemas the exports are validated against are unmodified copies (xlink.xsd is CRLF).
graph-io/test/conformance/schemas/** -text -diff

# Visual review baselines are Git LFS objects (design/visual-testing/design.md section 7): plain-git
# image history is permanent and would grow every clone. Review records and story settings files
# (visual-baselines/**/*.json) stay plain git. Without git-lfs, run `git lfs install` first
# (visual-review/README.md, "Setup").
visual-baselines/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text

# The design mocks' screenshots are Git LFS objects for the same reason as the visual baselines; the
# HTML beside each one is the source and regenerates it.
design/ui/**/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
